{"Lines 25-27 inject the literal string 'refresh_token' as a dummy value when no refresh_token is present, which for Office365 overwrites the valid existing refresh_token via the spread on line 264 of CalendarService.ts, breaking subsequent token refreshes": 0.5806657671928406, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses [z.string().toString()] as computed property keys which evaluate to '[object Object]' instead of dynamic key matchers, causing the schema to strip all properties except access_token from parsed token data when APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is true": 0.7418694496154785, "In salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts, the getClient method refreshes the OAuth token and saves it to the database, but then creates the jsforce.Connection using the stale credentialKey.access_token and credentialKey.instance_url from the original credential instead of the freshly obtained accessTokenParsed.data values": 0.9636335968971252, "In zoho-bigin/lib/CalendarService.ts, refreshOAuthTokens on line 93 is passed credentialId (credential.id, the database row ID) instead of credential.userId, causing incorrect user lookup when credential sync is enabled": 0.9601752161979675}